WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.409
Good morning Hank, it's Friday. It's question
Friday, the day that I answer real questions

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:05.310
from real Nerdfighers. Let's get right to
it.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.730
Favorite joke?
Billy was a chemist's son, but Billy is no

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.150
more. What he thought was H2O Was H2SO4. Hey!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.460
What's your take on the Oxford comma?
Lovely comma space, unintrusive comma space,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.449
and absolutely necessary.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:20.320
Can you cart wheel?
*attempts cart wheel*

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.320
No.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.210
Who the F is Hank?
Hank is a city of just over 3000 people in

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.330
southern South Dakota known for it's pheasant
season.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.630
Do you fit into those wooden shoes in the
background?

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.630
Kinda.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:34.510
Other than heights, what are you afraid of?
Hmmmm...Geese, Mice, and oblivion.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.550
What did you and Hank fight about when you
were kids?

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.800
We primarily fought about whether I should
be able to rewrite the rules of games we were

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.579
playing while we were playing them in order
to ensure my victory. I felt that this was

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:47.670
not only my privilege as on older brother,
but also my responsibility, where as Hank

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.920
was kind of a wuss about it.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.110
John, how are you so cool for a nerd?
I don't agree with your premise and as evidence

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:57.989
for my case I would like to present you with
middle school me. Thanks for getting me those

00:00:57.989 --> 00:00:59.050
glasses mom.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.990
How can I find other Nerdfighters at my school?
My recommendation is to acquire or make a

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:04.990
DFTBA shirt.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:08.250
What does DFTBA mean anyways?
It means Don't Forget To Be Awesome.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.530
What would you name your puppy sized elephant?
I would call him Lewis and we would be the

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.560
best of friends.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.230
How can I get all these old Nerfighter jokes
if I'm a new Nerdfighter?

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.790
If you listen to Hank's music, read my books,
watch some old videos, and hang around for

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:20.850
a while you'll get it all eventually.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.939
How do you feel about the Kindle?
I don't really care how people read, I care

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:24.939
if they read.

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:27.159
Is your next book really narrated by a girl?
Yes.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:29.329
Will you ever right another book with David
Levithan?

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:32.360
Maybe, but in the mean time you can just read
David Levithan's amazing new book that he

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.979
wrote by himself, The Lover's Dictionary.
Link below.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:38.049
Favorite Mountain Goats song?
Raskolnikov felt sick, but he couldn't say

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:42.310
why when he saw his face reflected in his
victims twinkling eye.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.780
What Mountain Goats album should I start with?
I forgive you for ending your sentence with

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.860
a preposition and present you with a recommendation
in the dooblydoo.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.820
Will we ever see the Yeti?
I don't know, let me consult my edition of

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:58.210
Yeti Researcher volume 24 number 8. This thing
has ads. It has a snowmobile ad. I guess that

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.210
makes sense, I mean if you're going to be
finding the Yeti you might need a snowmobile.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.500
Yea, no I don't think you're ever going to
see the Yet.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.060
Would you date a girl more intelligent than
yourself?

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.399
Yes, in fact I married one.

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:10.560
Your headdesk was lame.
That's not a question, but thank you for your

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.700
constructive criticism. Hold on, I'll try
to do better. Ahhhhhhhh...Headdesk! *Headdesk,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:27.590
followed by sigh and other noises* Ohhh, excessive
headdesk.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.690
The rest of today's video will be performed
while concussed.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.820
Is the world going to end in 2012?
I excessively headdesked and now I don't remember

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:35.820
your question.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.960
What is the purpose of a water tower?
I used to know the answer to that; it involves

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.770
gravity, but then I excessively headdesked
and forgot.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:44.670
What's your middle name?
I don't know, is today Tuesday? Did I hit

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:45.670
my head earlier?

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:49.420
How old are you?
Why am I sitting in front of a video camera?

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.730
When will your zombie apocalypse novella be
finished?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.070
Hopefully within a week or so, it's terrible
and I want to finish it so I can go back to

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.530
my real book, but I need some zombie killing
scenarios. So if you know of any can you please

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.670
leave them in the dooblydoo?

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:05.160
Hank there are a bunch of other questions,
but I think I actually gave myself a concussion,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:19.190
so I will see you uhhh...Man, that, yea...Monday,
I will see you on Monday.

